'''''Cistus lasianthus''''', the '''Lisbon false sun-rose''' or '''woolly rock rose''', is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] Cistaceae, [[native plant|native]] to the [[Iberian Peninsula]] (Portugal, western Spain and southwestern France) and Northwest Africa (Morocco).<ref>{{cite web |title=Halimium lasianthum (Lam.) Spach |url=http://www.floraiberica.es/floraiberica/texto/pdfs/03_066_02_Halimium.pdf |publisher=[[Flora Iberica]] |access-date=4 December 2021}}</ref> It is a spreading [[evergreen]] shrub growing to {{convert|1|m|ft|0|abbr=on}} tall by {{convert|1.5|m|ft|0|abbr=on}} wide, with grey-green leaves and bright yellow flowers in spring. The flowers may have a maroon blotch at the base of each petal.<ref name=RHSAZ>{{cite book|title=RHS A-Z encyclopedia of garden plants|year=2008|publisher=Dorling Kindersley|location=United Kingdom|isbn=978-1405332965|pages=1136}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=''Halimium lasianthum''|url=http://www.cistuspage.org.uk/Halimium%20lasianthum.htm|work=Cistus & Halimium website|access-date=27 July 2013|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131005075926/http://www.cistuspage.org.uk/Halimium%20lasianthum.htm|archive-date=5 October 2013|df=}}</ref>

In cultivation this plant requires a sandy soil and full sun.<ref>{{cite web|title=''Halimium lasianthum''|url=http://apps.rhs.org.uk/plantselector/plant?plantid=900|archive-url=https://archive.today/20130423222927/http://apps.rhs.org.uk/plantselector/plant?plantid=900|url-status=dead|archive-date=April 23, 2013|work=RHS Plant Finder|publisher=Royal Horticultural Society|accessdate=27 July 2013}}</ref>

